%I A066367 #20 Jul 28 2026 23:52:34
%S A066367 5,7,11,49,169
%N A066367 The floor(prime(n)/n)-perfect numbers, where prime(n) denotes the n-th prime and f-perfect numbers for an arithmetical function f are defined in A066218.
%C A066367 There do not seem to be any more terms. There are no terms between 170 and 10^5.
%C A066367 No terms between 170 and 10^8. - _Žiga Pirc_, Jul 24 2026
%H A066367 Joseph L. Pe, <a href="https://vixra.org/abs/2503.0165">On a Generalization of Perfect Numbers</a>, J. Rec. Math., 31(3) (2002-2003), 168-172.
%t A066367 f[x_] := Floor[Prime[x] / x]; Select[ Range[2, 10^3], 2 * f[ # ] == Apply[ Plus, Map[ f, Divisors[ # ] ] ] & ]
%o A066367 (PARI) p = primes([1, prime(10^8)])
%o A066367 v = vector(10^8, n, floor(p[n]/n))
%o A066367 for(n = 1, 10^8, s = 0; fordiv(n, d, s+=v[d]); if(2*v[n] == s, print(n))) \\ _Žiga Pirc_, Jul 24 2026
%Y A066367 Cf. A038605, A066218.
%K A066367 nonn,more,changed
%O A066367 1,1
%A A066367 _Joseph L. Pe_, Dec 21 2001
